<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Gaozong of Song</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1107–1187</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Zhao Gou</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Gaozong of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>, Zhao Gou, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-huizong">Emperor Huizong</a>, escaped the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaifeng">Kaifeng</a> in 1127 and was enthroned as the first emperor of the Southern Song. He established the capital at Lin'an (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hangzhou">Hangzhou</a>) and in 1141 made peace with the Jin, executing the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yue-fei">Yue Fei</a>. He abdicated in 1162.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozong-of-song.jpg" alt="Emperor Gaozong of Song" width="320" height="558" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Song_Gaozong.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
